4pt]\nF_{y} &= F\\sin\\theta = 250\\sin30^{\\circ}=250(0.5)=\\boxed{125\\;{\\rm N\\;(upward)}}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n### 2. Normal reaction force  \n\n\\[\nN = mg - F_{y}= (50)(9.81)-125 = 490.5-125 = \\boxed{365.5\\;{\\rm N}}\n\\]\n\n### 3. Kinetic‑friction force  \n\n\\[\nf_k = \\mu_k N = 0.20(365.5)=\\boxed{73.1\\;{\\rm N}}\\qquad(\\text{opposes motion})\n\\]\n\n### 4. Net horizontal force  \n\n\\[\nF_{\\text{net}} = F_{x} - f_k = 216.5 - 73.1 = \\boxed{143.4\\;{\\rm N}}\n\\]\n\n### 5. Acceleration of the component  \n\n\\[\na = \\frac{F_{\\text{net}}}{m}= \\frac{143.4}{50}= \\boxed{2.87\\;{\\rm m/s^{2}}}\n\\]\n\n### 6. Work done by the applied force  \n\n\\[\nW_{\\text{app}} = F\\,s\\cos\\theta = 250(12)\\cos30^{\\circ}=250(12)(0.8660)=\\boxed{2.60\\times10^{3}\\;{\\rm J}}\n\\]\n\n(Equivalently \\(W_{\\text{app}} = F_x s = 216.5\\times12\\).)\n\n### 7. Work done by kinetic friction  \n\n\\[\nW_{\\text{fric}} = -f_k s = -(73.1)(12)=\\boxed{-8.77\\times10^{2}\\;{\\rm J}}\n\\]\n\n### 8. Net work on the component  \n\n\\[\nW_{\\text{net}} = W_{\\text{app}}+W_{\\text{fric}}\n               = 2598\\;{\\rm J} - 877\\;{\\rm J}\n               = \\boxed{1.72\\times10^{3}\\;{\\rm J}}\n\\]\n\n(Also \\(W_{\\text{net}} = F_{\\text{net}} s = 143.4\\times12\\).)\n\n### 9. Change in kinetic energy  \n\n\\[\n\\Delta KE = W_{\\text{net}} = \\boxed{1.72\\times10^{3}\\;{\\rm J}}\n\\]\n\n### 10. Final velocity (starts from rest)  \n\n\\[\nv = \\sqrt{2as}= \\sqrt{2(2.87)(12)} = \\sqrt{68.84}= \\boxed{8.30\\;{\\rm m/s}}\n\\]\n\n(Consistent with \\(\\tfrac12 m v^{2}=1720\\;{\\rm J}\\).)\n\n### 11. Average power developed by the applied force  \n\nFirst find the time of travel:\n\n\\[\ns = \\tfrac12 a t^{2}\\;\\;\\Longrightarrow\\;\\; t = \\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{a}}\n      = \\sqrt{\\frac{24}{2.87}} = \\boxed{2.89\\;{\\rm s}}\n\\]\n\nAverage power:\n\n\\[\n\\overline{P}= \\frac{W_{\\text{app}}}{t}\n            = \\frac{2598\\;{\\rm J}}{2.89\\;{\\rm s}}\n            = \\boxed{9.0\\times10^{2}\\;{\\rm W}}\\;(\\approx 0.90\\;{\\rm kW})\n\\]\n\n(Alternatively \\(\\overline{P}=F_{x}\\,v_{\\text{avg}} = 216.5\\,(v/2)=216.5\\,(4.15)=898\\;{\\rm W}\\).)\n\n---\n\n### Summary of results  \n\n| Quantity | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Normal reaction force \\(N\\) | **365\u202fN** |\n| Kinetic‑friction force \\(f_k\\) | **73\u202fN** (opposing motion) |\n| Net horizontal force \\(F_{\\text{net}}\\) | **143\u202fN** |\n| Acceleration \\(a\\) | **2.87\u202fm\u202fs⁻²** |\n| Work by applied force \\(W_{\\text{app}}\\) | **2.60\u202fkJ** |\n| Work by friction \\(W_{\\text{fric}}\\) | **‑0.877\u202fkJ** |\n| Net work \\(W_{\\text{net}}\\) | **1.72\u202fkJ** |\n| Change in kinetic energy \\(\\Delta KE\\) | **1.72\u202fkJ** |\n| Final speed \\(v\\) | **8.3\u202fm\u202fs⁻¹** |\n| Average power of the applied force \\(\\overline{P}\\) | **≈\u202f0.90\u202fkW** |\n\nAll calculations use \\(g = 9.81\\;{\\rm m/s^{2}}\\) and are rounded to three significant figures where appropriate.'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tool_choice': {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'CalculationOutput'}}, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'CalculationOutput', 'description': '', 'parameters': {'properties': {'selected_tool': {'description': "The engineering tool/function selected to solve the problem. Example: 'calculate_beam_stress'", 'type': 'string'}, 'calculation_result': {'additionalProperties': True, 'description': "The result returned by the engineering calculation tool. Example: {'stress': 25e6, 'unit': 'Pa'}", 'type': 'object'}, 'validation_result': {'additionalProperties': True, 'description': "Stores the result of validating the inputs and calculation. Example: {'valid': True, 'warnings': []}", 'type': 'object'}, 'explanation': {'description': 'The final human-readable explanation generated for the user. Contains 